  message: "GOVERNANCE APPROVAL REQUESTED -- comment text only, no PR opened.\n\nTHE ASK. Correct five comment sites in `scripts/auto-pr` (lines 1085, 1494,\n2326) and `.githooks/reference-transaction` (lines 22 and 35). No behaviour\nchanges, no new tests. Both files are governance, so even a comment diff waits\non your word.\n\nWHY IT IS NOT HOUSEKEEPING. These comments say the recover marker covers \"fetch\n+ post-merge fast-forward\". It covers the whole run, CI poll included -- up to\n~45 minutes for auto-pr and up to its `ci_timeout` for do_sync. WI-pohir then\nproposed detecting a leaked marker by age, reasoning that \"no auto-pr fetch+ff\nwindow is that long\". That is a faithful reading of these comments, and shipped\nas written it would have false-alarmed on every auto-pr with slow CI. I caught\nit only because I measured the span instead of reading it, and that is not\nsomething to depend on a second time.\n\nTHE SMALLER HALF. reference-transaction:22 still sends an operator to a manual\n`tracker recover` for the clean/stash gap. AGENTS.md now sends them to\n`reconcile`, because `recover` restores the journal and leaves the repo behind\nthe upstream -- which is exactly how the other two steps get skipped.\n\nDELIBERATELY SEPARATE FROM WI-gokuv, which touches the same two files. WI-gokuv\nmay end up `wont_do` if its fd-inheritance premise fails under test; these\ncomments should be corrected either way, and I do not want one to hold the other\nhostage.\n\nALREADY DONE WITHOUT WAITING: the tracker-package half of the same\nmis-description -- `cli.py` and `test_reconcile.py`, both saying \"around its own\nfetch\" -- is not governance and is being corrected now."  # 7d15
